> -------------------------------------------------------------------------
> File: Smap_sea_sedim.xyz 
> 
> Frid: 5 min x 5 min for 50.000N -  85.000N / 00.000E - 50.000E
>
> Data: latitude, longitude, conductance, thickness (dummy values)
>
> Compiled:
>  "Toivo Korja" <toivo.korja@gsf.fi> / 2000-04-12
> Original compilation:
>  "Nick A. Palshin" <palshin@geo.sio.rssi.ru> / 2000-01-15
>
> This file contains conductances of the sediments at the sea bottom.
> Additional column is introduced for thickness of the sediment layer,
> but in current version dummy zero values is used.
>
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------
> 
> Seas include:
> - Atlantic Ocean
> - Barents Sea
> - White Sea
> - Baltic Sea (including Gulf of Finland, Gulf of Bothnia and Bothnian Bay)
> - Lake Ladoga
> 
> 
> ASCII file containing LON, LAT and S. (5 min resolution).
> It is based on interpolation of 1 degree sediment map
> (see G. Laske and G. Masters, A Global Digital Map of Sediment
> Thickness, EOS Trans. AGU, 78, F483, 1997).
> 
> 
> The procedure was as follows:
> 1. Calculating sediment conductance using sediment thickness for 1
> degree mesh.
> 2. Interpolatung (Kriging method) it to 5 min mesh.
> 3. Inserting zeros to continenal areas using 5 min altitiude database as
> a mask.
> 
>
> ------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Columns:
> --------
> latitude (degrees), longitude (degrees), conductance (S), thickness (m)
>
> ------------------------------------------------------------------------
